# Never apply line-ending conversion to binary files.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true corrupts them on checkout. This was
# caught on manuscript/chapters_3_to_5.pdf: a fresh clone received 746
# extra bytes from LF->CRLF expansion and a broken xref table. Git's
# automatic binary detection looks for NUL bytes near the start of a
# file and had classified that PDF as text.

*.pdf  binary
*.pt   binary
*.npy  binary
*.mat  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico  binary
*.zip  binary
